in switzerland on the coast of lake  geneva sits the quiet town of montreal  it was a place where people went to  retire to lots of lots of tea shops and  little old ladies kind of place but on  december 4th 1971  a giant fire at the local concert hall  took hold  eventually leading this man my name is  roger glover i'm the bass player of deep  purple  to help write this song  so let's rewind a bit  deep purple just arrived in switzerland  planning to record their next album  machine head at a local concert venue  but they couldn't start until frank  zappa and the mothers of invention  finished their show that afternoon being  big fans we went to the matinee show  and watched the mothers of invention in  frank about an hour or so into the show  someone had fired a flare gun into the  ceiling  the concert abruptly ended and once  everyone exited safely within five  minutes  flames everywhere and it raged it was  just a massive fire and went on  in fact it went on through the night  the concert hall was reduced to ashes  deep purple eventually found a new space  and feverishly recorded their sixth  studio album there was one problem  though we realized that we were a song  short so the band improvised and had an  idea why don't we write a song about  what happened to us here in montreux the  whole adventure of trying to make a  record and a place burning down  just then roger remembered a vision he  had back in montreal about  a day or two after the fire i woke up  one morning with the with four words  that i'd apparently said out loud they  seemed to be hanging in the room as i  opened my eyes  i kind of said to myself what did i just  say  smoke on the water or something like  that  smoke in the water well that could be  the story of the fire and so we sat down  and literally wrote the words to it in  probably about 15 minutes  smoke on the water  fire in the sky  the song became a surprise hit for the  band but also taught roger a valuable  lesson you're at your best when you're  not trying too hard  i think you have more fun when you when  you don't know that anything's going to  come of it  you
 

